er b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1407221#post1407221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Batman.<br /> <br /> Conan.<br /> <br /> Sherlock Holmes.<br /> <br /> Montgomery Scott.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irene Adler<br /> <br /> Who\u2019s Montgomery Scott?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T04:14:04-07:00","id":1407263,"title":"","content":"Conan is obviously a dawn who uses integrity and melee. And oh yes, mighty thews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T05:08:24-07:00","id":1407274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1407263#post1407263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conan is obviously a dawn who uses integrity and melee. And oh yes, mighty thews.</div> </div> </div> </div>He could just as easily be an Athletics Supernal Night. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T05:14:16-07:00","id":1407275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1407274#post1407274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He could just as easily be an Athletics Supernal Night. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hell yeah. He was also pretty stealthy. <br /> <br /> But with that level of charisma, (being able to steal a person's warband beneath him) he can be a zenith! It even fits with his durability! I mean, that 'survive being stuck in the sun while crucified' is obviously something out of Resistance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T09:06:45-07:00","id":1407310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1407260#post1407260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Irene Adler<br /> <br /> Who\u2019s Montgomery Scott?</div> </div> </div> </div>Commander Montgomery Scott, best known for his many years of service aboard the USS Enterprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T10:12:48-07:00","id":1407322,"title":"","content":"Oh, you mean Scotty from the original Star Trek. Cool. Thanks.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I guess he\u2019d make a pretty good Exalted. Maybe a Sidereal? Like a Chosen of Mercury (patron of travelers)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T13:57:39-07:00","id":1407365,"title":"","content":"Craft was a Serenity Ability in 1e and 2e, actually, so I'd peg him as a Joybringer <i>if</i> I was making him as a Sidereal. Though I'd be more inclined to put his miraculous patch-jobs in the hands of either a Twilight or a No Moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T15:06:07-07:00","id":1407386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1407365#post1407365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Craft was a Serenity Ability in 1e and 2e, actually, so I'd peg him as a Joybringer <i>if</i> I was making him as a Sidereal. Though I'd be more inclined to put his miraculous patch-jobs in the hands of either a Twilight or a No Moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. I think Twilight would definitely work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T18:16:32-07:00","id":1407410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1407260#post1407260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irene Adler</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me wrong, Irene Adler <i>is</i> a badass, but I think it'd actually be more appropriate to the original narrative if she was a &quot;mere&quot; mortal.<br /> <br /> Sherlock underestimates her when he forms his plan to trick her into revealing the location of the troublesome photograph; ultimately his failure to consider that she could be on his level intellectually, is what leads to her discovering his identity and escaping.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I like my Exalted best when mortals can remind them from time to time that they're not gods.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-10-2020, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T20:02:04-07:00","id":1407431,"title":"","content":"Elric of Melnibone (Twilight or Defiler, your call)<br /> <br /> Kane (by Karl Edward Wagner), clearly an Abyssal, probably a Daybreak<br /> <br /> Rand al'Thor (Twilight or Zenith with a SERIOUS case of Throwback Flaw)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26206-sadric-of-ysyr","name":"Sadric of Ysyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26206_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T00:49:40-07:00","id":1407461,"title":"","content":"For alchemicals, you can have Robocop, Inspector Gadget, Darth Vader, Gizmo duck)<br /> <br /> for lunars, you can havepretty much every furry disney hero (like the whole cast of Chip &amp; Dale Rescue Rangers, Talespin), the ninja turtles, Usagi Yojimbo (very fitting) <br /> <br /> for solars, most fantasy human anime protagonists, like any of the good guys from DBZ<br /> <br /> <br /> you can fit pretty much anything or anyone into exalted with a bit of imagination","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T03:52:30-07:00","id":1407479,"title":"","content":"Two candidates occur to me, both from the realm of sci-fi novels:<br /> <br /> <b>Emile Khadaji</b>, the Man Who Never Missed, from Steve Perry\u2019s Matador series, is definitely a Zenith (okay, possibly an Eclipse) Caste Solar. Waging a quiet, one-man war against an oppressive, all-powerful interstellar tyranny? Check. Carefully documenting his guerrilla strikes for maximum impact on the public, once his deeds are exposed, triggering a systems-wide revolution? Check. Glorious martyrdom, making him a figure of legend forevermore? Check. Sidereal sifu who teaches him Celestial Martial Arts because he knows he\u2019s destined to be the teacher of the savior of humanity? Check, and mate.<br /> <br /> <b>Jame Retief</b>, of the Corps Diplomatique Terrestrienne (CDT), from Keith Laumer\u2019s excellent Retief series. He\u2019s as Eclipse as one could be, using insight, language mastery, diplomacy, sociology, and psychology to forever stymie the Soviet-like Groaci in their quest to assimilate the known universe under their croaking rule. <br /> <br /> And he does all this while nominally bound by the CDT\u2019s obsession with protocol and hierarchy. That\u2019s the same CDT that wastes time, energy, and political will in nonsense like the following:<br /> <br /> <i> &quot;A most perceptive observation, Chester,&quot; Earlyworm said, bestowing a 24-w (Gracious Condescension) leavened with a hint of 7-y (Expectation of Great Things in Due Course) on the lucky bureaucrat, at which his fellow underlings around the table were quick to bombard him with approbation, ranging from Faintlady's 12.7-x (Knew You Had It In You, Fella) to Felix's more restrained 119-a (We're All Pulling For You, Lad), to which he responded with a shy 3-v (Modest Awareness of Virtue).<br /> &quot;In fact,&quot; Earlyworm interjected a Cold Return to Objectivity (91-s) into the lightning interplay of ritual grimacing ...</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","user":"39Steps","date":". 08-11-2020, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T04:26:01-07:00","id":1407482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1407410#post1407410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't get me wrong, Irene Adler <i>is</i> a badass, but I think it'd actually be more appropriate to the original narrative if she was a &amp;quot;mere&amp;quot; mortal.<br /> <br /> Sherlock underestimates her when he forms his plan to trick her into revealing the location of the troublesome photograph; ultimately his failure to consider that she could be on his level intellectually, is what leads to her discovering his identity and escaping.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I like my Exalted best when mortals can remind them from time to time that they're not gods.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. So like a heroic mortal. VERY good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T04:46:43-07:00","id":1407674,"title":"","content":"Any character played by Bruce Lee","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""