_ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1408310#post1408310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Xena and Gabrielle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A Dawn and her Changing Moon mate...although they may work even better as a Full Moon and her Eclipse mate!<br /> <br /> Team Leverage makes for an almost textbook example of a Modern Solar Circle:<br /> <br /> Nate: Eclipse<br /> Sophie: Zenith<br /> Elliot: Dawn<br /> Hardison: Twilight<br /> Parker: Night","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T08:38:31-07:00","id":1416269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1408086#post1408086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no way in hell Vader is an Alchemical. The suit does nothing except help him breathe, and the Lightsaber is just an artifact sword. No part of his power set comes from his relationship to technology. It's just set dressing.<br /> <br /> Vader is an Abyssal combat sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree that's the best fit for him, but I could also see him as an Infernal! Palpatine definitely has &quot;Fiend&quot; written all over him...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T21:30:33-07:00","id":1416410,"title":"","content":"The Slayer*: Dawn Caste<br /> Willow: Twilight Caste (with a real dangerous Limit Break)<br /> Rupert Giles: Chosen of Secrets<br /> <br /> <br /> *Could be Buffy, Faith, or Kendra","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T21:51:19-07:00","id":1416412,"title":"","content":"Mentors who make for great Sidereal Mentors/Sifu:<br /> <br /> -Yoda/Obi-Wan<br /> -Oogway/Soothsayer (Kung Fu Panda)<br /> -Morpheus<br /> -The Ancient One<br /> -Dakuan (the priest/spy from Ninja Scroll)<br /> <br /> Any others?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T21:59:57-07:00","id":1416413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1416412#post1416412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mentors who make for great Sidereal Mentors/Sifu:<br /> <br /> -Yoda/Obi-Wan<br /> -Oogway/Soothsayer (Kung Fu Panda)<br /> -Morpheus<br /> -The Ancient One<br /> -Dakuan (the priest/spy from Ninja Scroll)<br /> <br /> Any others?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Who's that guy? <br /> <br /> The guy in that Karate kid movie. The guy who had the student learn from doing chores. I say it would certainly be within theme for a Sidereal sifu to be able to train someone several dots in an ability by having them do something utterly unrelated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T22:14:49-07:00","id":1416416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1416413#post1416413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who's that guy?<br /> <br /> The guy in that Karate kid movie. The guy who had the student learn from doing chores. I say it would certainly be within theme for a Sidereal sifu to be able to train someone several dots in an ability by having them do something utterly unrelated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mr. Miyagi! And 2E gave us a standalone MA Charm that does just that...I think it's in Ink Monkeys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T22:20:02-07:00","id":1416418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1416416#post1416416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mr. Miyagi! And 2E gave us a standalone MA Charm that does just that...I think it's in Ink Monkeys?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pah! Martial Arts charms. It should be in lore!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T22:28:06-07:00","id":1416421,"title":"","content":"I think there's a similar charm in 3E Solar Lore...? I always wanted a charm that mirrored the story where the Buddha enlightens one of his followers...by simply holding up a flower. Not sure how that'd work mechanically, tho...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T22:29:51-07:00","id":1416422,"title":"","content":"Like Accelerator, I happen to feel disdainful about it being a Charm, but for different reasons; namely, writing up something cool as a Charm tends to remove the possibility of it being able to be done mundanely, and I feel like this feat is something that should be possible for mortals to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T22:38:17-07:00","id":1416429,"title":"","content":"I see your point, but disagree, largely because having a feat as a Charm doesn't automatically *invalidate* it as a mundane feat. A mortal sifu can still do it as a Stunt; all it means is that, by applying Essence, an Exalt can do it better (or, more accurately, be assured of success). TBH, if a mortal teacher pulls it off, it is actually MORE impressive because of that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T22:52:47-07:00","id":1416431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1416422#post1416422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Accelerator, I happen to feel disdainful about it being a Charm, but for different reasons; namely, writing up something cool as a Charm tends to remove the possibility of it being able to be done mundanely, and I feel like this feat is something that should be possible for mortals to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>How? I feel like something like this should be something mortals can't do. How would you even put it in the system? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think there's a similar charm in 3E Solar Lore...? </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Yup. there's one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T00:33:55-07:00","id":1416439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1416429#post1416429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your point, but disagree, largely because having a feat as a Charm doesn't automatically *invalidate* it as a mundane feat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t say \u201cautomatically.\u201d I said \u201ctends to.\u201d Ghosts, for example, got a Charm making them able to produce Ghost-Blooded offspring, and <i>with</i> it, lost the ability to produce Ghost-Blooded offspring in any other way. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s not the only example, either. Just one I\u2019m rather bitter about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1416431#post1416431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How? I feel like something like this should be something mortals can't do. How would you even put it in the system?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201dThe system\u201d <b>already has</b> stuff for how training works, and loath as I am to use the Air Bud defense, the details for training don\u2019t preclude the possibility of not initially realizing that you\u2019re being trained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-02-2020, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T18:31:50-07:00","id":1418457,"title":"","content":"With every book, Harry Dresden is more obviously an exigent of Winter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T22:00:15-07:00","id":1418480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1416412#post1416412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mentors who make for great Sidereal Mentors/Sifu:<br /> <br /> -Yoda/Obi-Wan<br /> -Oogway/Soothsayer (Kung Fu Panda)<br /> -Morpheus<br /> -The Ancient One<br /> -Dakuan (the priest/spy from Ninja Scroll)<br /> <br /> Any others?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Kisuke Uahara<br /> <br /> Rufus (B&amp;T's EA)<br /> <br /> Hiko Seijuro<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 10-16-2020, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T17:57:50-07:00","id":1418743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1418457#post1418457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With every book, Harry Dresden is more obviously an exigent of Winter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably call Dresden a Twilight, but his Celestial sorcerous initiation was a pact with Winter. His toughness and respect from Winter fae would be merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/513-gatts","name":"Gatts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T04:32:08-07:00","id":1419553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gatts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1418743#post1418743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd probably call Dresden a Twilight, but his Celestial sorcerous initiation was a pact with Winter. His toughness and respect from Winter fae would be merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since access to magic can be bought as an advantage, I'd say he was a heroic mortal for most of his career - until narrowly avoiding becoming an infernal, and then getting sponsored by a deity. <br /> <br /> As for others... <br /> <br /> Someone mentioned The Ancient One. That space folding she does in the prologue is how I imagine sidereal martial arts are supposed to look like. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I'm thinking about Darkseid. Between his &quot;crush the Universe under his boot because he IS tyrrany&quot;, attitude, his power level, and his body being an avatar of his real self that takes a whole dimension to himself... would it be a stretch to call him a Yozi? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T12:22:41-07:00","id":1419621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1418457#post1418457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With every book, Harry Dresden is more obviously an exigent of Winter.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I mean, with him being Starborn, I'd say a Chosen of Endings with Winter-based Sorcerous initiation.<br /> <br /> On another note, plenty of Fire Emblem characters are Dragonblooded, no doubt about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T23:53:50-07:00","id":1419924,"title":"","content":"If we're diving into pulp urban fantasy, than I suggest John Taylor who debuted in <i>Something From the Nightside </i>and its 12 book <b>Nightside</b> series. Without going into spoilers, he's an Exigent of an scifi-magic city (the titular Nightside), where its always 3am and serves as a neutral ground between Heaven, Hell, the Fair Folk, some of the Other Things, numberless small gods, and is full of timeslips- portals to the past and a wide variety of alternate futures. Your just as likely to get mugged by a junkie with a laspistol as you are to meet a succubus turning tricks or pack of werewolves. I highly recommend it. <br /> <br /> John's power is to find things. Lost people, lost items, etc. He can &quot;find&quot; the bullets in your gun, or if he's in a bad mood, your fillings or even your source of magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T20:32:30-07:00","id":1420209,"title":"","content":"Thunderbolt Fantasy has some really, really accurately depicted Exalted characters for me.There's Shang Bu Huan (Dawn, Supernal Brawl using a martial art like Single Point Shines Into the Blade), Lin Xue Ya/Enigmatic Gale (Elder Chosen of Battle), Mie Tien Hai (Abyssal, Dusk) and Di Kong/Lou Zhen Jie (Infernal, Malfean Scourge with a demon relic girlfriend-YES, you read that last part right).<br /> <br /> I'm just not sure what Lang Wu Yao is. I'm inclined to think Zenith because he has a talking artifact weapon instrument and sing well enough to parry a dragon's breath back in it's face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407126-what-fictional-characters-could-believably-be-exalted-in-hiding?p=1415360#post1415360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been playing Hades for a few days and Zagreus is the archetypal Dawn. Although considering the game is escaping the Underworld hes probably an Abyssal.<br /> <br /> No spoilers but there are 2 entities which are akin to Primordials as well</div> </div> </div> </div>The only reason I didn't have Zagreus pegged as a Dawn is because most of his powers come from blessings from the Olympians, which kind of fall outside the gamut of a Dawn even with copious abuse of Divine Mantle.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the other two are definitely Primordial material. Especially the one who just casually offers to rewrite fate for your (eventual, after enduring a curse) benefit, when every other character treats the Fates as immutable.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23788\" data-vbnamecard=\"23788\">Braininthejar</a> Oh yes, he's definitely the Yozi kind of character. The sort of force of nature so overwhelming it's honestly not explained very well why he hasn't slaughtered the Justice League especially since at the moment he's canonically slain the whole League and their planet on numerous parallel Earths. The funny thing is if you've ever looked at the other New Gods, especially post-New 52, he's quite possibly the only one who fits the bill in practice because he's just so much more successful than the rest. Who are just, not really treated very respectfully at all by their own source material considering recently one was literally used as a food bribe to placate a cosmic demon. That was his son Orion too.<br /> <br /> Recently he even restored himself AND Apokolips to full power into the Sphere of the Gods after they were both nearly wiped from existence from an even more powerful cosmic being* getting unleashed. Heck, his daughter Grail was written as a Crisis-level individual and she has human blood (She's half-Amazon. It's...not explained well)<br /> <br /> *Allegedly Perpetua is...not very well written and the scope of her power is more told than shown a lot of times.<br /> <br /> I'd bring up the Batman Who Laughs but honestly the sheer badly written plot armo-I mean scope of what he does probably belongs more in Nobilis 3e than anything. Specifically, as a Warmain.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26317\" data-vbnamecard=\"26317\">Critian Caceorte</a> There's some very odd offhanded lines about Starborn in the latest books (Drakul-one of the guys who could take on Mab in a 1v1 and win (if she was the kind of character who did 1v1 fights-being one apparently, Mavra wanting to sacrifice Harry to the &quot;stars and stones&quot;, the Starborn only coming about every 666 years) that make me wonder if being Starborn is actually more Infernal than we all initally thought.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8830_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8830\" data-vbnamecard=\"8830\">Sorcerous Overlord</a> Technically he'd be the Exigent of <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i>Lilith</i> now, wouldn't he? The Nightside is merely where she invested her power after all.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","user":"Organ Boy","date":". 10-26-2020, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]